:: MakeSimpleTools [childhood]
# Crafting Beginnings

You approach your father, who is working on crafting a new spear. He smiles when he sees your interest.

"Would you like to learn?" he asks, and when you nod eagerly, he sets aside his work and finds a small piece of wood for you.

"We'll start with something simple," he says. "A digging stick for finding roots."

He shows you how to select the right piece of wood - straight, without too many knots - and how to use a stone scraper to remove the bark. Then he demonstrates how to sharpen one end by carefully scraping it against a rough stone.

The work is harder than it looks. Your small hands struggle with the tools, but your father is patient, guiding you when needed and praising your efforts.

<<if gameUtils.hasSkillLevelIncreased("toolMaking")>>
  <div class="skill-message">
    <span class="skill-increase">Your tool making skill has improved!</span>
  </div>
<</if>>

<<link "Continue working on your digging stick">>
  <<set $skills.toolMaking += 0.2>>
  <<goto "FinishDiggingStick">>
<</link>>

<<link "Ask about making other tools">>
  <<goto "LearnAboutTools">>
<</link>>